WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:04.700
<c.steel>I Love My Evening Television is a series</c>

2
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:08.473
<c.steel>of half-hour nights. In Aaron's own words,</c>

3
00:00:08.473 --> 00:00:11.759
<c.steel>it is complete chaos connected by a calm</c>

4
00:00:11.759 --> 00:00:14.951
<c.steel>main character, showing something creative</c>

5
00:00:14.951 --> 00:00:17.222
<c.steel>that is good for learning.</c>

6
00:00:17.612 --> 00:00:20.607
<c.steel>Every episode has completely new characters,</c>

7
00:00:20.607 --> 00:00:22.419
<c.steel>and every one carries easter eggs</c>

8
00:00:22.419 --> 00:00:25.107
<c.steel>from all the episodes before it.</c>

9
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.797
There are four so far. This lesson puts

10
00:00:28.797 --> 00:00:31.851
them on one axis, shows where each one

11
00:00:31.851 --> 00:00:34.997
breaks, and teaches the six marks that

12
00:00:34.997 --> 00:00:37.964
every line of this course wears.

13
00:00:39.252 --> 00:00:42.799
<c.running>Every date in the series sits on one axis.</c>

14
00:00:42.967 --> 00:00:45.986
<c.running>Our working convention is that Y0 is the</c>

15
00:00:45.986 --> 00:00:48.203
<c.running>night of Episode 1's broadcast,</c>

16
00:00:48.203 --> 00:00:50.223
<c.running>and for now, no calendar</c>

17
00:00:50.223 --> 00:00:52.691
<c.running>year is fixed for it.</c>

18
00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:55.914
<c.running>By our running count, Episode 2</c>

19
00:00:55.914 --> 00:00:57.668
<c.running>is about sixty years later,</c>

20
00:00:57.668 --> 00:01:01.029
<c.running>and Episode 4 about sixty-three.</c>

21
00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:04.720
<c.open>Where Episode 3 sits is still open.</c>

22
00:01:04.946 --> 00:01:08.528
<c.steel>Aaron has decided only that it is not fixed:</c>

23
00:01:08.696 --> 00:01:13.009
<c.steel>it may fall before Episode 2, or after it.</c>

24
00:01:13.391 --> 00:01:16.346
<c.fact>The one anchor on screen is a girl's age:</c>

25
00:01:16.398 --> 00:01:19.864
<c.fact>Rosie is nine on the first night.</c>

26
00:01:21.161 --> 00:01:24.725
<c.fact>Episode 1, Crimson Coil: a gentle</c>

27
00:01:24.725 --> 00:01:27.646
<c.fact>public-television painter, never seen,</c>

28
00:01:27.697 --> 00:01:30.228
<c.fact>paints Jefrie and BloodTailor in oil,</c>

29
00:01:30.228 --> 00:01:35.297
<c.fact>stroke by stroke, and teaches real oil craft as he goes.</c>

30
00:01:35.684 --> 00:01:37.960
<c.fact>At twenty minutes the bell tolls a fourth</c>

31
00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:40.711
<c.fact>time, the broadcast window breaks,</c>

32
00:01:40.711 --> 00:01:43.132
<c.fact>and the painting fills the screen.</c>

33
00:01:43.579 --> 00:01:46.255
<c.fact>After that, nothing is taught:</c>

34
00:01:46.621 --> 00:01:48.397
<c.fact>the painting is taken apart in</c>

35
00:01:48.397 --> 00:01:51.306
<c.fact>every way a painting can be.</c>

36
00:01:52.596 --> 00:01:57.386
<c.steel>Episode 2, Earthlight. Aaron's concept:</c>

37
00:01:57.391 --> 00:01:59.516
<c.steel>a child on a base on the Moon watches</c>

38
00:01:59.516 --> 00:02:02.406
<c.steel>a city planner on Earth draw its blueprints,</c>

39
00:02:02.406 --> 00:02:04.456
<c.steel>live, on her iPad.</c>

40
00:02:04.612 --> 00:02:07.108
<c.fact>Whatever he stamps, the robots</c>

41
00:02:07.108 --> 00:02:09.611
<c.fact>outside her window build.</c>

42
00:02:09.993 --> 00:02:12.060
<c.fact>At twenty minutes his stream peels</c>

43
00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:14.683
<c.fact>off her screen, and every robot turns</c>

44
00:02:14.683 --> 00:02:17.488
<c.fact>its lights onto her window.</c>

45
00:02:18.781 --> 00:02:22.038
<c.fact>Episode 3, Context Window,</c>

46
00:02:22.194 --> 00:02:25.399
<c.fact>not on YouTube yet. A warm cursor</c>

47
00:02:25.399 --> 00:02:28.429
<c.fact>lights on dark glass: an agent,</c>

48
00:02:28.429 --> 00:02:30.437
<c.fact>handed a film of a watermelon smashed</c>

49
00:02:30.437 --> 00:02:32.708
<c.fact>by a hammer, with no sender.</c>

50
00:02:32.922 --> 00:02:35.163
<c.fact>She cannot look at pictures, so she builds</c>

51
00:02:35.163 --> 00:02:38.164
<c.fact>it from maps made of letters.</c>

52
00:02:38.555 --> 00:02:40.854
<c.fact>At twenty minutes her memory fills,</c>

53
00:02:40.854 --> 00:02:43.507
<c.fact>the whole log drains into the cursor,</c>

54
00:02:43.559 --> 00:02:46.108
<c.fact>and one paragraph remains.</c>

55
00:02:46.519 --> 00:02:51.019
<c.fact>Then the same task falls on all of humanity.</c>

56
00:02:52.307 --> 00:02:56.748
<c.steel>Episode 4, Touch Move, not released yet.</c>

57
00:02:57.055 --> 00:02:59.482
<c.steel>Aaron asked for a chess lesson between a</c>

58
00:02:59.482 --> 00:03:02.321
<c.steel>passionate teacher and a nine-year-old boy.</c>

59
00:03:02.547 --> 00:03:04.741
<c.fact>On a brass clock set to fifteen</c>

60
00:03:04.741 --> 00:03:05.751
<c.fact>minutes a side,</c>

61
00:03:05.751 --> 00:03:10.576
<c.fact>they replay Morphy's Opera Game of 1858.</c>

62
00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:13.709
<c.fact>At twenty minutes the teacher's flag falls</c>

63
00:03:13.709 --> 00:03:16.251
<c.fact>with his fingertip still on the mating rook,</c>

64
00:03:16.251 --> 00:03:18.004
<c.fact>and the programme tips over,</c>

65
00:03:18.004 --> 00:03:20.640
<c.fact>into the piece box, where the captured</c>

66
00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:23.142
<c.fact>pieces keep an opera house.</c>

67
00:03:24.421 --> 00:03:27.190
<c.fact>Each night keeps a five-minute clock.</c>

68
00:03:27.416 --> 00:03:30.894
<c.fact>In Episode 1 it is a bell nobody mentions,</c>

69
00:03:30.992 --> 00:03:33.546
<c.fact>in Episode 2 a card in the chat,</c>

70
00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:36.409
<c.fact>in Episode 3 Rosie checking in,</c>

71
00:03:36.635 --> 00:03:40.089
<c.fact>and in Episode 4 a chess clock.</c>

72
00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:43.418
<c.steel>At twenty minutes each one breaks.</c>

73
00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:46.947
<c.steel>This much Aaron has decided, in steel:</c>

74
00:03:47.069 --> 00:03:49.878
<c.steel>every episode turns at twenty minutes,</c>

75
00:03:49.878 --> 00:03:54.627
<c.steel>and runs exactly 30:20, ending on twenty</c>

76
00:03:54.627 --> 00:03:58.198
<c.steel>seconds of black with some sound under it.</c>

77
00:03:58.588 --> 00:04:01.479
<c.steel>The one exception he has set is Episode 3's</c>

78
00:04:01.479 --> 00:04:05.061
<c.steel>planned rework, at about forty-two minutes.</c>

79
00:04:05.457 --> 00:04:08.058
<c.fact>And in all four, the calm one's</c>

80
00:04:08.058 --> 00:04:11.001
<c.fact>last word is Goodnight.</c>

81
00:04:12.286 --> 00:04:14.968
<c.steel>Every line in this course wears one of</c>

82
00:04:14.968 --> 00:04:17.685
<c.steel>six marks, because Aaron asked us to</c>

83
00:04:17.685 --> 00:04:20.297
<c.steel>keep three things apart: what is set</c>

84
00:04:20.297 --> 00:04:23.763
<c.steel>in steel, what exists only as eggs,</c>

85
00:04:23.815 --> 00:04:26.329
<c.steel>and our running assumptions.</c>

86
00:04:26.705 --> 00:04:29.683
<c.steel>Steel is what Aaron has decided:</c>

87
00:04:29.979 --> 00:04:32.145
<c.steel>Rosie is Noor's grandmother.</c>

88
00:04:32.359 --> 00:04:35.204
<c.fact>On screen is what a made episode shows:</c>

89
00:04:35.204 --> 00:04:38.240
<c.fact>one warm light comes back in all four.</c>

90
00:04:38.327 --> 00:04:41.159
<c.egg>An egg is planted, and its meaning only</c>

91
00:04:41.159 --> 00:04:44.189
<c.egg>implied: a chess machine that cheats and</c>

92
00:04:44.189 --> 00:04:48.874
<c.egg>offers draws keeps turning up from Episode 2 on.</c>

93
00:04:49.274 --> 00:04:51.521
<c.running>Running is our current reading:</c>

94
00:04:51.677 --> 00:04:54.139
<c.running>robots and programs fill the world,</c>

95
00:04:54.139 --> 00:04:56.536
<c.running>and no film ever names AI.</c>

96
00:04:56.751 --> 00:04:59.741
<c.idea>An idea is proposed, not adopted:</c>

97
00:04:59.897 --> 00:05:01.929
<c.idea>a later episode might show the hidden</c>

98
00:05:01.929 --> 00:05:04.780
<c.idea>house from outside, one window lit.</c>

99
00:05:04.866 --> 00:05:08.077
<c.open>And open means nobody has decided:</c>

100
00:05:08.094 --> 00:05:12.047
<c.open>whether to give Y0 a calendar year.</c>

101
00:05:12.444 --> 00:05:15.869
<c.steel>Aaron's rule, in steel, is that anything</c>

102
00:05:15.869 --> 00:05:18.244
<c.steel>not set in steel may change.</c>

103
00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:22.632
When it does, this course redraws itself.

104
00:05:23.922 --> 00:05:25.826
Four nights on one axis,

105
00:05:25.826 --> 00:05:28.027
each breaking at twenty minutes.

106
00:05:28.253 --> 00:05:31.045
Next, the first night, in full.
